  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The interhalogen compounds can be prepared by the direct combination or by the action of halogen on lower interhalogen compounds. The product formed depends upon some specific conditions, For e.g.,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>diluted</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>with</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>water</mi></mrow></mfenced></munder></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mi>excess</mi></mfenced></munder></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>HBrO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>HF</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HBrO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is bromic acid, hence, the salt is bromate. And interhalogen compound is called halate.</p></blockquote>",
